-- tests-independent: written by an independent test author from the German text alone.
-- Every expected value is from ANSWERS.md (written before any .l4 file was opened), never from the encoding's output.
-- One #ASSERT per scenario (a, b ... where one scenario has two facts); each comment gives the scenario number and the provision.
-- Convention for the expected word: JUST TRUE = the text says yes; JUST FALSE = the text says no in its own words; NOTHING = not covered.
-- Scenarios with no function to ask are listed as GAP at the end.  A failing assertion is a finding and is left failing.

-- A. Art 90 and 91: final and partial decisions
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #1 Art 90: a decision that ends the proceedings is appealable
#ASSERT `Art 90 the appeal is admissible against the decision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #2 Art 90 alone: a decision that does not end the proceedings; Guide: grant not closed with only
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #3 Art 91(a): partial decision, claims can be judged independently
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #4 Art 91(a): partial decision, claims cannot be judged independently; Guide: wenn condition fails, periods ruling (b)
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #5 Art 91(b): decision ends the proceedings for only some of the co-litigants
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #6 Art 90 (with 91(b) off): decision ends the proceedings for all co-litigants

-- B. Art 92: jurisdiction and recusal
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #7 Art 92(1): separately notified interim decision on jurisdiction
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #8 Art 92(1): separately notified interim decision on a recusal request (the seat has one flag for both)
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #9 Art 92(1): jurisdiction decision NOT separately notified; Guide: scope limit with no only (ruling (c))
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) my decision on jurisdiction or recusal can be challenged later` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #10 Art 92(2): separately notified jurisdiction decision not appealed, can it be challenged later? flat negative
#ASSERT `Art 92(2) my decision on jurisdiction or recusal can be challenged later` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #11 Art 92(2): recusal decision appealed and lost, challenge again later? flat negative
#ASSERT `Art 92(1) the appeal is admissible against the preliminary or interlocutory decision on jurisdiction or recusal` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #12 Art 92(1): interim decision on evidence is outside Art 92(1); Guide: scope limit

-- C. Art 93: other interim decisions
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #13 Art 93(1)(a): other separately notified interim decision, irreparable disadvantage
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #14 Art 93(1)(b): no irreparable harm; granting would immediately end the case and save much evidence cost
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #15 Art 93(1): neither (a) nor (b); Guide: wenn condition fails, periods ruling (b)
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #16 Art 93(1)(b): immediate final decision but no significant saving; Guide: wenn ... und damit fails
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #17 Art 93(2): interim decision in international legal assistance in criminal matters with irreparable harm; Guide: flat negative nicht anfechtbar
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #18 Art 93(2): interim decision in asylum with irreparable harm; Guide: flat negative
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #19 Art 93(2) reservation: extradition detention, Art 93(1) condition met
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #20 Art 93(2) reservation: extradition detention, Art 93(1) conditions not met; Guide: sofern condition fails
#ASSERT `Art 90 to 93 the appeal is admissible against my decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #21 Art 93(2) reservation: seizure of assets in legal assistance, Art 93(1) condition met
#ASSERT `Art 93(3) my other preliminary decision can be challenged by the appeal against the final decision` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #22 Art 93(3): not appealable on its own, affects the content of the final decision
#ASSERT `Art 93(3) my other preliminary decision can be challenged by the appeal against the final decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #23 Art 93(3): appealable but no use made, affects the content
#ASSERT `Art 93(3) my other preliminary decision can be challenged by the appeal against the final decision` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #24 Art 93(3): does not affect the content; Guide: soweit read as as long as (arguable)  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-18: was EQUALS JUST FALSE; AMBIGUOUS (assumed, not ruled; the encoder's reading stands, marginal reading for a lawyer): Art 93(3) "soweit" read as a limit on its own wording (NOTHING, the encoder's fork F3) against read as a "where" condition that fails (JUST FALSE, periods ruling (b))
#ASSERT `Art 93(3) my other preliminary decision can be challenged by the appeal against the final decision` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #25 Art 93(3): appeal was admissible and used; Guide: Ist ... oder condition fails

-- D. Art 94: denial and delay of justice
#ASSERT `Art 94 the appeal lies against the unlawful refusal or delay of my decision` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #26 Art 94: unlawful delay of an appealable decision
#ASSERT `Art 94 the appeal lies against the unlawful refusal or delay of my decision` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #27 Art 94: unlawful refusal of an appealable decision
#ASSERT `Art 94 the appeal lies against the unlawful refusal or delay of my decision` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #28 Art 94: the delayed decision is not appealable; Guide: grant limited in its own wording
#ASSERT `Art 94 the appeal lies against the unlawful refusal or delay of my decision` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #29 Art 94: lawful delay; Guide: grant limited in its own wording

-- E. Art 95: Swiss law
#ASSERT `Art 95 I can complain of the violation of this source of law` FALSE `federal law` EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #30 Art 95(a): federal law
#ASSERT `Art 95 I can complain of the violation of this source of law` FALSE `international law` EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #31 Art 95(b): international law
#ASSERT `Art 95 I can complain of the violation of this source of law` FALSE `cantonal constitutional rights` EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #32 Art 95(c): cantonal constitutional rights
#ASSERT `Art 95 I can complain of the violation of this source of law` FALSE `cantonal provisions on political voting rights and on popular elections and votes` EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #33 Art 95(d): cantonal voting-rights and election provisions
#ASSERT `Art 95 I can complain of the violation of this source of law` FALSE `intercantonal law` EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #34 Art 95(e): intercantonal law
#ASSERT `Art 95 I can complain of the violation of this source of law` FALSE `another source of law` EQUALS NOTHING  -- #35 Art 95: ordinary cantonal statute law; Guide: list not closed with only
#ASSERT `Art 95 I can complain of the violation of this source of law` FALSE `another source of law` EQUALS NOTHING  -- #36 Art 95: a municipal bylaw; Guide: list not closed with only

-- F. Art 96: foreign law
#ASSERT `Art 96 I can complain about the application of foreign law` FALSE `foreign law was not applied as Swiss private international law prescribes` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #37 Art 96(a): foreign law not applied, pecuniary matter
#ASSERT `Art 96 I can complain about the application of foreign law` FALSE `foreign law was not applied as Swiss private international law prescribes` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #38 Art 96(a): foreign law not applied, non-pecuniary matter
#ASSERT `Art 96 I can complain about the application of foreign law` FALSE `foreign law that Swiss private international law makes applicable was applied wrongly` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #39 Art 96(b): foreign law applied wrongly, non-pecuniary
#ASSERT `Art 96 I can complain about the application of foreign law` FALSE `foreign law that Swiss private international law makes applicable was applied wrongly` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #40 Art 96(b): foreign law applied wrongly, pecuniary; Guide: sofern condition fails
#ASSERT `Art 96 I can complain about the application of foreign law` FALSE `another complaint about foreign law` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #41 Art 96: foreign law applied although PIL does not call for it; Guide: list not closed with only

-- G. Art 97: facts
#ASSERT `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #42 Art 97(1): manifestly incorrect and could be decisive
#ASSERT `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #43 Art 97(1): incorrect but not manifestly; Guide: nur ... wenn
#ASSERT `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #44 Art 97(1): manifestly incorrect but cannot be decisive; Guide: nur ... wenn
#ASSERT `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #45 Art 97(1): rests on a violation of Art 95 and could be decisive
#ASSERT `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #46 Art 97(2): accident insurance, money benefit refused, incomplete (not manifestly)
#ASSERT `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #47 Art 97(2): military insurance, money benefit awarded, incorrect (not manifestly)
#ASSERT `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #48 Art 97: accident insurance benefit in kind, incorrect but not manifestly; Guide: nur in 97(1), 97(2) is limited to Geldleistungen
#ASSERT `Art 97 I can complain about the finding of the facts` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #49 Art 97: disability insurance money benefit, incorrect but not manifestly; Guide: nur in 97(1)

-- H. Art 98: provisional measures
#ASSERT `Art 98 I can raise this complaint against the decision on provisional measures` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #50 Art 98: precautionary measure, constitutional right
#ASSERT `Art 98 I can raise this complaint against the decision on provisional measures` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #51 Art 98: precautionary measure, ordinary federal law; Guide: closed with nur
#ASSERT `Art 98 I can raise this complaint against the decision on provisional measures` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #52 Art 98: a final decision on the merits; Guide: scope limit with no only (ruling (c))

-- I. Art 99: new submissions
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) I may put forward the new fact or new evidence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #53 Art 99(1): new fact that only the lower decision gave occasion for
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) I may put forward the new fact or new evidence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #54 Art 99(1): evidence that was available before; Guide: nur so weit
#ASSERT `Art 99(2) my new claim is admissible` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #55 Art 99(2): new request; Guide: flat negative
#ASSERT `Art 99(2) my new claim is admissible` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE  -- #56 Art 99(2): new request even though the lower decision gave cause; Guide: flat negative, no exception
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) I may put forward the new fact or new evidence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #57 Art 99: a new legal argument (not fact, evidence or request); Guide: silent

