-- L. Art 102: exchange of submissions
#ASSERT `Art 102(1) the Court must send my appeal to this recipient and set a time limit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #93 Art 102(1): service necessary, recipient is the lower instance
#ASSERT `Art 102(1) the Court must send my appeal to this recipient and set a time limit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE  -- #94 Art 102(1): service necessary, recipient is a party, a participant or an authority entitled to appeal (one flag for the four)
#ASSERT `Art 102(1) the Court must send my appeal to this recipient and set a time limit` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING  -- #95 Art 102(1): service not necessary; assumed reading (a duty whose soweit is unmet)  -- RECONCILED 2026-11-18: was EQUALS JUST FALSE; AMBIGUOUS (assumed, not ruled; the encoder's reading stands, marginal reading for a lawyer): a duty whose "soweit erforderlich" is unmet is one of the six case-by-case questions (Guide, last ruling of 2026-11-05); the encoder answered NOTHING and the reader JUST FALSE
